==Trivia ==
*The [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musket musket] is a muzzle-loaded long gun that appeared as a smoothbore weapon in the early 16th century, at first as a heavier variant of the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arquebus arquebus], capable of penetrating [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plate_armour plate armour]. By the mid-16th century, this type of musket gradually disappeared as the use of heavy armour declined, but muskets continued as the generic term for smoothbore long guns until the mid-19th century. In turn, this style of musket was retired in the 19th century when [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rifled_musket rifles] became common, which were more accurate than smoothbore muskets and could inflict more severe injuries.
** In the Arabic and Persian language settings of the game, the Musketeer's name translates to "Knight" and "Riflewoman" respectively.
*The Musketeer [[Cards|card]] could be a reference to the fourth Musketeer in the novel "''[https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Three_Musketeers The Three Musketeers]''", D'Artagnan, who was never considered to be in the group.
*Unlike her regular counterpart, the Evolved Musketeer has a cape in both her card image and in [[Basics of Battle|battle]].
*The Musketeer’s Evolution is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
*Before the Musketeer's Evolution's release, the Evolved Musketeer's sniper attack time interval was decreased to 1 second (from 1.5 seconds).

